    interpreter_lazy_same_name_class_entry_ambiguous_type_2026_11_27, fixing, p3sweep4-20261127, 2026-11-27T19:35:40Z, 2026-11-27T19:35:40Z, open, "wave9"

    interpreter_lazy_same_name_class_entry_ambiguous_type_2026_11_27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4-61127: the doc's literal module-scope shape was GREEN at tip; the live failing shape is BLOCK-SCOPED imports (use inside a fn body / it block loads lazily and never records an owner binding): semantic: ambiguous type Thing: defined in pa.spl, pb.spl and none of them is imported by <entry> - in default JIT mode the same shape segfaulted (exit 139); the doc's only-compiler-paths claim was inaccurate (fixtures paths fail identically). Root cause: module_cache.rs:2237 resolve_class_in_scope scoped_walk(owner) errors on 2+ candidates; module-scope imports record entry bindings via flattened import-binding markers so the walk succeeds; block-scoped/lazy imports bind the constructor into the local env + flat MODULE_GLOBALS but record no owner binding, so the walk dead-ends even though the entry imported exactly one class. Fix (module_cache.rs only, 22 lines): after the owner walk misses on a shared name, resolve through runtime_imported_class(classes, name) before erroring - if the flat global surface binds name to a Value::Constructor{class_name}, return the caller's flat class slot ONLY when its identity still matches (def.name == class_name): owner-exact names resolve exactly, an overtaken slot keeps the loud ambiguity error (no fail-open). Verification on the scratch build: block-use in main, block-use in a called fn, and the doc's compiler.* shape all print the expected values; module-scope imports unchanged; spec test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_block_scoped_import_spec.spl RED 0/1 (exact ambiguous error) to GREEN 1/1; neighbours identical pass/fail on patched vs unpatched (their failures pre-exist - stale bin/simple shell-outs); cargo test -p simple-compiler --lib module_cache 31 passed 0 failed. Residuals: the JIT lane segfault on the block-use shape recorded as NEW BUG jit_block_use_same_name_class_segv_2026-11-27 (hir/lower TAKEN by another agent - fix direction: record_owner_binding in the block-use arms as evaluation_helpers.rs:72 does for module-scope uses, plus a hir/lower crash-site investigation); the pure-Simple lane is covered by the separately filed pure_simple_interpreter_class_table_keyed_by_bare_name_2026_11_27 (no self-hosted binary here to run its side). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_block_scoped_import_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_mixed_lane_spec.spl"
    interpreter_lazy_same_name_class_entry_ambiguous_type_2026_11_27, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep4: module-scope shape was GREEN at tip; the live shape is BLOCK-SCOPED lazy imports (ambiguous type error in the interpreter; SEGV exit 139 on the JIT lane). Root cause: module_cache.rs:2237 scoped_walk errors on 2+ candidates; block-scoped/lazy imports bind the constructor into the local env + flat MODULE_GLOBALS but record no owner binding. Fix (module_cache.rs, 22 lines): after the owner walk misses on a shared name, resolve through runtime_imported_class before erroring - return the caller's flat class slot ONLY when its identity still matches the constructor's class_name (owner-exact; an overtaken slot keeps the loud ambiguity error, no fail-open). Spec same_name_class_block_scoped_import RED 0/1 to GREEN 1/1; cargo test module_cache 31/31; neighbours identical to baseline (pre-existing failures are stale-bin shell-outs). Residuals: JIT-lane block-use SEGV recorded as NEW BUG jit_block_use_same_name_class_segv_2026-11-27 (fix direction: record_owner_binding in the block-use arms + hir/lower crash-site investigation); pure-Simple lane covered by pure_simple_interpreter_class_table_keyed_by_bare_name_2026_11_27. close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_block_scoped_import_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/interpreter/same_name_class_mixed_lane_spec.spl"
